# This example is inactive. Copy it to .owner-override to enable it:
# cp .owner-override.example .owner-override
# Use dotenv-style KEY=value syntax. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# Values may be unquoted or enclosed in matching single or double quotes.
# Keep one active OWNER_OVERRIDE assignment; alternatives below are examples.

# pause: stop gating and process work; just do the requested task.
OWNER_OVERRIDE=pause

# bypass-review: skip reviewer requirements when merging.
# Replace the active assignment above with:
# OWNER_OVERRIDE=bypass-review

# reset: discard the in-flight plan and epic state and start fresh.
# Preserve implementation work; do not replay prior approvals.
# Replace the active assignment above with:
# OWNER_OVERRIDE=reset

# Combine modes with commas:
# OWNER_OVERRIDE="pause,bypass-review"

# Disable file-based overrides for this repo with an explicit empty value:
# OWNER_OVERRIDE=
# This setting applies only to the project containing this root file.
# Never share or symlink this file between projects, or put it in your home.
# Overrides in other directories or environment variables do not apply.
# If a key is repeated, the last assignment in that file wins.

# Removing .owner-override disables file-based overrides for this project.
# Chat/Slack overrides also apply only to the project they were given for.
# This is agent-readable configuration, not a shell script. Do not source it.
# No command execution or environment-variable expansion is performed.
# Overrides skip checks; they never turn skipped checks into passing results.
# Record Owner-Override: <mode> with a timestamp in the commit trailer or PR
# description when an override is used. Platform permissions still apply.
